  "title": "Kaitai Shinsho (New Book of Anatomy)",
  "summary": "Kaitai shinsho, a five-volume Japanese anatomy book, was published in Edo in 1774 by Suharaya Ichibei. It was translated from the Dutch Ontleedkundige tafelen (1734), itself a translation of Kulmus's German Anatomische Tabellen (1732), by Sugita Genpaku, Maeno Ryotaku, Nakagawa Jun'an and Katsuragawa Hoshu, with illustrations by Odano Naotake. Translation work ran from 1771 to 1774.",
